B = [
('Clarks','Europe','1950s-present','footwear','In the style of Clarks, understated British comfort with a relaxed, lived-in handsomeness. Forms are soft, rounded and unfussy, with generous plump outlines, gentle stitched seams and thick panelled edges that feel easygoing and honest. Surfaces are velvety napped suede and smooth polished hide in sand, tobacco brown, olive, navy and black, paired with a pale honey gum tone for contrast bases. Details are minimal, with tidy topstitching, plain stitched details and quiet metal fittings, never showy ornament. The wordmark is a bold, flowing, hand-drawn cursive script in black or white on deep teal or cream. Natural, earthy, practical and quietly friendly, with a worn-in, softly creased finish.'),
('Pendleton','North America','1900s-present','textiles','In the style of Pendleton, cosy, graphic wool heritage from the American Northwest. Thick, tightly woven wool in bold geometric motifs such as stepped diamonds, zigzags, chevrons, triangles, banded stripes and large plaids, arranged in symmetrical, repeating bands. Palette is saturated rust red, turquoise, mustard gold, forest green, navy, cream and black, balanced in warm earthy blocks. Edges are bound or finished with neat fringe, and surfaces have a soft brushed nap and a sturdy, woolly hand. Emblem is a rectangular woven or printed label in deep blue with gold border, framed in a double outline, with bold gold serif capitals and a small wool sheep roundel. Rustic, warm, durable and handcrafted.'),
('Lanvin','Europe','1920s-present','fashion','In the style of Lanvin, graceful Parisian elegance with a tender, romantic polish. Soft, fluid, gently draped forms are trimmed with satin ribbons, oversized bows, ruffles and delicate gathers. Fine silks, satin, taffeta and crisp black grosgrain are enriched with jewelled embroidery, crystal beading, gold-toned metal and sparkling ornamental trim. Palette is powder blue, rose, lilac, cream, black and soft metallic gold, often as tonal harmonies or dramatic black and white. Emblem is a black silhouette of two figures in flowing gowns, a simple stylised line drawing set above widely spaced, refined serif capitals. Chunky gold chain links and bold embroidered lettering add a modern twist to the classic polish.'),
('Schiaparelli','Europe','1930s-present','fashion','In the style of Schiaparelli, witty surrealist couture where familiar things turn into clever visual jokes. Shocking hot pink is the signature colour, set against black, white, deep red, gold and rich jewel tones. Surfaces glitter with dense gold embroidery, faceted crystal clusters in pink, ruby and smoky grey, glossy lava glass and sculptural gilded metal in the shape of flowers, insects, lobsters, eyes, lips and anatomical forms. Silhouettes are sharp and structured, with strong shoulders and exaggerated, theatrical shapes. Optical illusion tricks make drawn or embroidered details mimic real ones. Ornaments are cast, enamelled and boldly oversized. Daring, artistic, glamorous, with a playful sense of the unexpected and a lavish gold flourish.'),
('Bottega Veneta','Europe','1970s-present','leather goods','In the style of Bottega Veneta, quiet luxury built on woven leather, thick flat ribbons interlaced in a tight, even, diagonal checkerboard weave that covers the whole surface of any object. The weave is supple, plump and slightly puffy, sometimes oversized and chunky, sometimes in fine knotted braids. Colours are rich and unshowy, such as pale powder blue, butter cream, parakeet green, lilac, burnt orange, taupe, chocolate, ruby red and black, often one saturated tone per piece. Metal details are sparse, polished gold or brass, in simple triangular, knot-like or bar forms. No external logos, only tiny discreet lettering. Understated, tactile, soft, sculptural and wonderfully crafted, with a sleek, modern, sophisticated calm.'),
('Mulberry','Europe','1970s-present','leather goods','In the style of Mulberry, British country heritage in rich, handsome leather. Naturally grained, softly pebbled and glossy hide in oak brown, chocolate, oxblood, forest green, navy, cream and tan, with contrast stitching and thick, sturdy edges. Surfaces are meant to soften and darken with use. Hardware is solid, heavy, antique brass and gold-toned metal, with a round, flat, domed or turn-style fitting in a classic, traditional look. The emblem is a leafy mulberry tree silhouette with a rounded, branching crown, shown in gold foil, embossed in tonal leather or on a round leather tab. Lettering is a refined, widely spaced serif in capitals. Timeless, practical, warm, quietly luxurious and countryside in spirit, with a confident, polished finish.'),
('Issey Miyake','East Asia','1970s-present','fashion','In the style of Issey Miyake, sculptural, weightless, inventive design that treats cloth as architecture. Fine, permanent, heat-set pleats run in crisp vertical, horizontal or zigzag rows, springing back into shape and catching light in rippling waves. Geometric forms such as tubes, cubes, circles and folded origami-like volumes expand and collapse flexibly. Textiles are lightweight polyester, crinkled and bonded technical weaves, sheer layers and stretchy jersey, shown matte and slightly shimmering. Palette alternates between muted charcoal, ivory, black and indigo and sudden bursts of neon lime, tangerine, cobalt, magenta and bright turquoise, with playful colour-blocking and bold abstract graphics. Lettering is plain, small, modern sans-serif. Clever, light, joyful, modern and wonderfully free.'),
('Comme des Garcons','East Asia','1980s-present','fashion','In the style of Comme des Garcons, deconstructed avant-garde design with asymmetric, deliberately distorted silhouettes, bulbous padded humps, oversized stiff shapes, exposed raw seams, unfinished frayed edges, holes, inside-out construction and layered mismatched panels. Dominant colour is severe black, then stark white, grey and a single shock of red, with occasional gingham, polka dot, tartan or flat pop prints. Materials are felt, crumpled cotton, boiled and distressed knits, lace, patent and cheap-looking synthetics treated as luxury. A simple, rounded, cartoon-like red heart emblem with two small oval eyes appears in black, red, green or white, above plain, bold, spaced, capital sans-serif lettering. Rebellious, intellectual and playfully strange, with beauty found in imperfection.'),
('Yohji Yamamoto','East Asia','1980s-present','fashion','In the style of Yohji Yamamoto, voluminous draped black design cut in oversized, asymmetric layers that hang away from the body so the silhouette becomes a dark, shadowy cloud. Materials are matte wool gabardine, crinkled cotton, heavy linen, felted wool and fluid jersey, with raw edges, oversized folds, tilted asymmetric edges, trailing hems and long scarf-like panels. Palette is overwhelmingly black, then charcoal, deep navy, off-white and rare blood red, sometimes with bold brush-stroke calligraphy marks, flowers or white graphic drawing scrawled across the dark surface. Tailoring is slouchy, androgynous, deliberately undone and poetic. Lettering is delicate, hand-drawn, slender handwriting-like script in white on black. Austere, moody, romantic and quietly rebellious..'),
('Kenzo','East Asia','1970s-present','fashion','In the style of Kenzo, joyful, colourful, folkloric design that mixes wide kimono-like volumes, loose smock shapes, patchwork, quilting and layered global prints within a single look. Large flowers, poppies, stripes, ginghams, checks and paisley are combined at clashing scale in saturated tomato red, yellow, turquoise, emerald, pink, purple and soft peach. Fabrics are cotton, soft jersey, knits and light gauzy weaves, cut in a relaxed, unstructured, unisex way. A fierce, embroidered or printed tiger face with open jaws and bold whiskers, bursting with floral detail and neon outlines, is the signature motif, set above spaced, thin, capital serif lettering in white, red or green. Cheerful, exotic, bold, playful and vividly graphic.'),
]
